ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/Two_Days_
 in_Mayaro_.png?cb=1792427147
DESCRIPTION:📚🚀🌴A Different Booklist & Goose Lane Editions are pro
 ud to present celebrated author Pamela Mordecai in conversation with journ
 alist Neil Armstrong for the launch of her new collection of Caribbean dia
 sporic short fiction\, TWO DAYS IN MAYARO!\nJamaican Canadian Pamela Morde
 cai's first short story collection\, PINK ICING received glowing reviews\,
  and her debut novel\, RED JACKET\, was shortlisted for the Rogers Writers
 ’ Trust Fiction Prize. She has published nine collections of poetry and 
 books for children. Weaving old time and contemporary stories\, TWO DAYS I
 N MAYARO\, Pamela's second collection of short fiction\, depicts the strug
 gles\, triumphs\, and humour of diaspora life\, creating a world powered b
 y unforgettable characters in language that sings.\nLook forward to a live
  reading by Pamela and a Q&A. Special guest writer Nalo Hopkinson will in
 troduce the author\, and Neil Armstrong will conduct the interview. See y
 ou there - #ReadDifferently!📚
LOCATION:BLACKHURST CULTURAL CENTRE
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BOOK LAUNCH: STOP ANTIBLACK RACISM\, by Nadia L. Hohn
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T160000
UID:bm-6699020261114@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/IMG_0094_
 _1_.jpeg?cb=1793551817
DESCRIPTION:📚🚀✊🏿Join award-winning author and educator Nadia L.
  Hohn for the launch of her latest release\, STOP ANTIBLACK RACISM: 8 WAYS
  TO ACT NOW.\nIn this practical book\, part of the Take Action Series by O
 rca Book Publishers\, Hohn identifies 8 steps for everyone - Black and non
 -Black people - to combat anti-Black racism. Together the steps offer read
 ers practical ways to overcome ignorance\, take a stand\, and get back up 
 after experiencing racism. The book includes a glossary and a list of reso
 urces for further exploration of the topic.\nNadia is one of Toronto's fav
 ourite authors\, bringing tremendous experience in education and publishin
 g to her work - this is her 12th book! She not only writes but sings\, pla
 ys the piano\, draws - a true artivist! Come celebrate Nadia\, her creativ
 ity\, and her newest achievement\, STOP ANTIBLACK RACISM\, a book that tea
 ches us all to take action! #ReadDifferently #socialjustice #CanLit #Afric
 anCanadian📚
LOCATION:Blackhurst Cultural Centre
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
